          "ImageDescription": {
            "value": "The Trevi Fountain (in italian <i>Fontana di Trevi</i>), Rome, Italy. The fountain is an 18th-century fountain in the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trevi_(rione_of_Rome)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Trevi (rione of Rome)\">Trevi</a> district in Rome, Italy, designed by Italian architect <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicola_Salvi\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Nicola Salvi\">Nicola Salvi</a> and completed by Giuseppe Pannini and several others. Standing 26.3 metres (86 ft) high and 49.15 metres (161.3 ft) wide, it is the largest <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baroque\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Baroque\">Baroque</a> fountain in the city and one of the most famous fountains in the world.",
